{"data":[{"amassId":"AMPC_Lfu8nE90d0f0A1ESvlN0rycfaNG","publicationNumber":"US-2016053011-A1","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US2016053011A1","applicationNumber":"US-201414781968-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"A1","familyId":"51898619","familyMembers":["AMPC_WhFS5hWmnOhJJnoORvohUKOb6pF"],"title":"Antibody specifically binding to her2","abstract":"The present invention relates to HER2 (Human Epidermal Growth Factor Receptor 2) antibodies to prevent or treat cancers. The antibodies of the invention binds specifically to HER2 over-expressed in cancer cells (particularly, breast cancer and stomach cancer cells), specifically to an epitope on HER2 being different from epitope for trastuzumab. The CDR sequences of the present antibodies exhibit low similarity to CDR sequences of publicly known HER2 antibodies, addressing that the CDR sequences are unique. The antibodies of the present invention in combination with trastuzumab kill cancer cells with significantly enhanced cytotoxicity and therefore very effective in therapy of cancer (particularly, breast cancer and stomach cancer). Without wishing to be bound by theory, the enhanced efficacies of the combined therapy would address that the antibodies of the present invention bind to epitope on HER2 being different from epitope for trastuzumab, and inhibit HER2 in a cooperative manner with trastuzumab.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["A61P5/26","A61P5/08","A61P5/46","A61P5/18","A61P35/00","A61P9/10","A61P5/40","A61P7/00","A61P17/02","A61P13/12","C07K16/2863","C07K2317/565","C07K16/32","A61K2039/505","A61K39/3955","A61K2039/507","A61K39/39558"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/28","A61K39/395"],"inventors":["LEE JONG-SEO","KIM KYU-TAE","LEE YOUNG-HA","LEE SOOK-YEON","HWANG IN-SIK","KO BONG-KOOK"],"assignees":["ABCLON INC"],"publicationDate":"2016-02-25","filingDate":"2014-05-14","grantDate":null,"priorityDate":"2013-05-16","citedPatents":[],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":0,"citedByCount":1},{"amassId":"AMPC_ZmDvVbyyxHM9wYolsD0cQu8KLgK","publicationNumber":"US-2022204644-A1","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US2022204644A1","applicationNumber":"US-202017606523-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"A1","familyId":"66625743","familyMembers":[],"title":"Combination of her2 antibodies","abstract":"The present invention is directed to HER2 antibodies directed against an epitope between amino acids 342-652 of human HER2 for use in the treatment of HER2 related disorders in combination with a second HER2 inhibitor. More specifically the invention relates to methods and uses of MAB270 or antibodies having the same CDRs as MAB270 in combination with trastuzumab or pertuzumab in HER2 positive cancer.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["A61K2039/505","A61K39/39558","C07K16/2863","A61K45/06","A61K2039/507","C07K2317/24","C07K16/32"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/32","C07K16/28","A61K45/06"],"inventors":["FISCHER STEPHAN"],"assignees":["MAB DISCOVERY GMBH"],"publicationDate":"2022-06-30","filingDate":"2020-04-29","grantDate":null,"priorityDate":"2019-05-02","citedPatents":["AMPC_3ymvn54EQnR7XPdsY1MIGExaPax","AMPC_EfZYG4bWC0i82aTrTsDBEbmzIZ2","AMPC_ZqLhwAHWYa7HtSUnOih65qFN0Kg"],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":10,"citedByCount":0},{"amassId":"AMPC_EfZYG4bWC0i82aTrTsDBEbmzIZ2","publicationNumber":"US-11091561-B2","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US11091561B2","applicationNumber":"US-201716099228-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"B2","familyId":"55919722","familyMembers":["AMPC_ZqLhwAHWYa7HtSUnOih65qFN0Kg","AMPC_J97AGkr2azPPzXT67muvgIytI0I","AMPC_WpqKmarzcFSTRshbd07LVPbcqv"],"title":"HER-2 binding antibodies","abstract":"The present invention relates to monoclonal antibodies that specifically bind to HER2, or a fragment or derivative thereof or a polypeptide that contains at least a portion of said antibody that is sufficient to confer specific HER2 binding to the polypeptide. Said antibodies bind to the human Fc receptor and induce FcR mediated signaling pathways. The antibodies according to the invention bind to a different epitope than trastuzumab. The invention also relates to the use of an antibody according to the invention in the treatment of a HER-2 mediated disease. The present invention also relates to a pharmaceutical composition comprising a pharmaceutically acceptable carrier and a therapeutically effective amount of the antibody according to the invention, and the use of said composition in the treatment of a HER-2 mediated disease.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["A61K2039/505","C07K2317/33","C07K2317/73","C07K16/32","C07K2317/24","A61P35/00","C07K2317/56","C07K2317/71","A61P35/04","C07K2317/565"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/32","A61P35/04","A61K39/00","A61P35/00"],"inventors":["FISCHER STEPHAN","BRANDT MICHAEL"],"assignees":["MAB DISCOVERY GMBH"],"publicationDate":"2021-08-17","filingDate":"2017-05-08","grantDate":"2021-08-17","priorityDate":"2016-05-06","citedPatents":["AMPC_5T4BoaPb51kHX3KSCYg138jXvS6","AMPC_VYH5TnWqq72hLuawg8C9ffrGErD","AMPC_5YKSeXdAkSDBzui8ay9TNzwpqvT","AMPC_4d6DV27t26PiBNRqPiartqPSslx","AMPC_W2OwxswKo7srxOeVTDY8imoKsfj","AMPC_7XYw9AygJHLKUHamJQaOe93iNN6"],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":10,"citedByCount":4},{"amassId":"AMPC_LQJ9zwhaFAj5DfHROw7VmfhdYMb","publicationNumber":"US-2021139605-A1","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US2021139605A1","applicationNumber":"US-201916969119-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"A1","familyId":"67621044","familyMembers":["AMPC_VHjVeOiVfEoDSp6b2TMK86YF6fx"],"title":"Anti-her2 antibodies","abstract":"Antibodies, antigen-binding fragments and polypeptides that bind to HER2 are disclosed, as well as nucleic acids and vectors encoding the same. Also provided are cells comprising the antibodies, antigen-binding fragments, polypeptides, nucleic acids and vectors, methods of making such molecules, and the use of such molecules for therapeutic applications.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["G01N33/5759","A61K40/4205","A61K40/31","A61K40/11","A61K2239/28","A61K39/39558","C07K2317/21","A61K2039/507","G01N2333/71","C07K2317/33","C07K2317/73","A61K2039/505","C07K2319/03","C07K2319/33","A61K2039/545","C07K2317/92","C07K16/32","C07K2317/622","A61P35/00"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/32","A61P35/00"],"inventors":["WANG CHENG-I","LOW LIONEL JIANRONG","GOH ANGELINE","LEE SANDY WEN-HSIN"],"assignees":["AGENCY SCIENCE TECH & RES"],"publicationDate":"2021-05-13","filingDate":"2019-02-12","grantDate":null,"priorityDate":"2018-02-13","citedPatents":["AMPC_IiNa3zUPgdU0lunzgg6hEhIjgGs"],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":3,"citedByCount":4},{"amassId":"AMPC_6Mj3RBjZttUEP1xNJuYtwNKoYNN","publicationNumber":"US-2023070306-A1","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US2023070306A1","applicationNumber":"US-202117406171-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"A1","familyId":"85386491","familyMembers":[],"title":"Monoclonal antibodies against her2/neu and uses thereof","abstract":"The present document describes an antibody or an antigen-binding fragment comprising three variable heavy domain complementarity determining regions (CDR) (CDR H1, H2 and H3) that binds specifically to Her2/Neu. The present invention also relates to pharmaceutical compositions, nucleic acid molecule, vectors, cells comprising the nucleic acid vectors, and methods of treating Her2/Neu associated diseases.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["C07K2317/56","C07K2317/622","C07K2317/92","C07K16/32","C07K2317/94","C07K2317/24","C07K2319/00","C07K2317/31"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/32"],"inventors":["MADIYALAKAN RAGUPATHY","WOO THOMAS"],"assignees":["ONCOQUEST PHARMACEUTICALS INC"],"publicationDate":"2023-03-09","filingDate":"2021-08-19","grantDate":null,"priorityDate":"2021-08-19","citedPatents":["AMPC_AtVShnZJODFylHPfG437MEMuki8"],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":0,"citedByCount":0},{"amassId":"AMPC_NMYwLlcDmraSyiFzNAYRlUdejqy","publicationNumber":"US-10167342-B2","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US10167342B2","applicationNumber":"US-201615249910-A","countryCode":"US","kindCode":"B2","familyId":"58190122","familyMembers":["AMPC_BXyiJzO39D4E5FvZBwA58EA9riw"],"title":"Production of hersintuzumab: a new humanized antibody against HER2 for cancer treatment","abstract":"A monoclonal anti-HER2 antibody is mutated on complementarity determining regions (CDRs) and framework regions. The VH domain of the antibody includes a portion of the amino acid sequence as SEQ ID NO: 1. The VL domain of the antibody includes a portion of the amino acid sequence as SEQ ID NO: 5.","language":"en","nonEnglishFallback":false,"cpcCodes":["A61K47/6851","C07K16/32","C07K2317/73","C07K2317/24","C07K2317/33","A61K47/48569"],"ipcCodes":["C07K16/30","A61K39/395","A61K39/00","C07K16/32","C07K16/28"],"inventors":["SHOKRI FAZEL","JEDDI-TEHRANI MAHMOOD","Mehdi Amiri Mohammad"],"assignees":["SHOKRI FAZEL","JEDDI TEHRANI MAHMOOD","Mehdi Amiri Mohammad"],"publicationDate":"2019-01-01","filingDate":"2016-08-29","grantDate":"2019-01-01","priorityDate":"2016-08-29","citedPatents":["AMPC_BvaDV9SK63WY3JsEVHPJQ5xJDqK","AMPC_y3RrgISv6L772S6q1k9ReqNGPo","AMPC_AnsALdgKjcwAL13cydgiAuIBxSR"],"priorityClaimNumbers":[],"parentPublicationNumbers":[],"childPublicationNumbers":[],"hasClaims":true,"hasDescription":true,"nplCount":0,"citedByCount":2},{"amassId":"AMPC_FGInVcvzYAdc52b74AtjQW9Klc9","publicationNumber":"US-8937159-B2","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US8937159B2","applicationNumber":"US-96937510-A","countryCode"